<section id="features" class="section"><div class="section-inner"><div class="section-kicker">One connected operating picture</div><h2>Designed around the work your teams actually do.</h2><p class="section-lead">From the first report in an examination hall to the final committee decision, BUK EIMS keeps the next action visible, legally grounded, and transparent.</p><div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon emerald-theme"><i class="fas fa-file-signature"></i></div><h3>Report with confidence</h3><p>Use a guided incident wizard with matriculation verification, course timetable cross-referencing, and multi-file evidence upload.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon azure-theme"><i class="fas fa-inbox"></i></div><h3>Work the queue</h3><p>Examination officers can triage incoming reports, request clarifications, initiate formal case dossiers, and balance ownership.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon purple-theme"><i class="fas fa-folder-open"></i></div><h3>See the whole case</h3><p>360° timelines bring invigilator statements, summons logs, student defenses, hearings, and sanctions into one structured dossier.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon amber-theme"><i class="fas fa-calendar-check"></i></div><h3>Coordinate hearings</h3><p>Manage committee summons, quorum attendance, digital hearing records, and recommended sanctions against the BUK Handbook.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon teal-theme"><i class="fas fa-chart-column"></i></div><h3>Understand patterns</h3><p>Monitor live trendlines, departmental heatmaps, repeat-offender analytics, and instant CSV exports for executive meetings.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon rose-theme"><i class="fas fa-file-pen"></i></div><h3>Never lose progress</h3><p>Save draft incident reports locally and remotely, resume work across devices, and ensure invigilators never lose field data.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section id="workflow" class="section workflow"><div class="section-inner workflow-grid"><div><div class="section-kicker">Clear path from report to resolution</div><h2>Every action has a designated place.</h2><p class="section-lead">A role-aware workflow gives invigilators, examination officers, HODs, deans, and committee members the exact tools they need at each stage.</p><div class="steps"><div class="step"><div class="step-number">01</div><div><h3>Capture the facts</h3><p>Record exam venue facts fresh from the hall with student matriculation validation and optional digital evidence uploads.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-number">02</div><div><h3>Triage and assign</h3><p>Examination officers vet incidents, clarify discrepancies, create official case records, and dispatch notifications.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-number">03</div><div><h3>Hear, decide, and close</h3><p>Committees review evidence, conduct formal hearings, deliberate verdicts, record sanctions, and generate Senate Working Papers.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="workflow-board"><div class="board-top"><span class="board-dot red"></span><span class="board-dot yellow"></span><span class="board-dot green"></span><div class="board-title">buk-eims / operations-console</div></div><div class="board-body"><div class="board-header"><strong>Live Operations Overview</strong><span class="board-badge"><span class="pulse-indicator"></span> Active Session</span></div><div class="board-stats"><div class="board-stat"><strong>12</strong><small>Triage queue</small></div><div class="board-stat"><strong>07</strong><small>Active cases</small></div><div class="board-stat"><strong>04</strong><small>Hearings</small></div></div><div class="faculty-breakdown"><div class="breakdown-title"><span><i class="fas fa-building-columns"></i> Cases by Faculty</span><span style="color:var(--buk-green)">94% Resolution Rate</span></div><div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-label">FCIT</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill green" style="width:75%"></div></div><span class="bar-val">12</span></div><div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-label">FNAS</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill blue" style="width:50%"></div></div><span class="bar-val">08</span></div><div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-label">SMS</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar-fill amber" style="width:25%"></div></div><span class="bar-val">04</span></div></div><div class="board-lines"><div class="board-line"><i class="fas fa-inbox" style="background:var(--buk-blue-soft);color:var(--buk-blue);border:1px solid var(--buk-blue-border)"></i><div><strong>Triage Queue</strong><small>12 new reports awaiting review</small></div><span class="pill blue-pill"><i class="fas fa-bolt"></i> Active</span></div><div class="board-line"><i class="fas fa-user-check" style="background:var(--buk-amber-soft);color:var(--buk-amber-dark);border:1px solid var(--buk-amber-border)"></i><div><strong>Hearing Summons</strong><small>Senate Chamber session scheduled</small></div><span class="pill amber-pill"><i class="fas fa-calendar"></i> Scheduled</span></div><div class="board-line"><i class="fas fa-file-export" style="background:var(--buk-green-soft);color:var(--buk-green-dark);border:1px solid var(--buk-green-border)"></i><div><strong>Senate Working Paper</strong><small>Memo BUK/SEN/2026/01 ready</small></div><span class="pill green-pill"><i class="fas fa-stamp"></i> Ratified</span></div></div></div></div></div></section>
<section id="institutional" class="section"><div class="section-inner"><div class="section-kicker">Built for institutional clarity</div><h2>A better experience for every role in the university.</h2><p class="section-lead">The interface is intentionally structured: zero confusing menus, transparent ownership, and high institutional integrity.</p><div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon emerald-theme"><i class="fas fa-person-chalkboard"></i></div><h3>For Invigilators</h3><p>Report quickly, save offline drafts, verify students, and upload evidence directly from examination halls.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon azure-theme"><i class="fas fa-briefcase"></i></div><h3>For Examination Officers</h3><p>Manage triage queues, assign investigating committees, track hearing summons, and generate gazette extracts.</p></article><article class="feature-card"><div class="feature-icon purple-theme"><i class="fas fa-scale-balanced"></i></div><h3>For Committees & Senate</h3><p>Review comprehensive case dossiers, cross-reference the BUK Handbook, record sanctions, and compile Senate papers.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="cta"><div class="cta-inner"><div class="eyebrow" style="justify-content:center"><i class="fas fa-building-columns"></i> BUK Examination Administration</div><h2>Make the next institutional action obvious.</h2><p>Sign in to access your role-tailored examination integrity workspace, report an incident, manage hearings, or monitor university analytics.</p><button id="cta-login" class="hero-button white"><i class="fas fa-arrow-right-to-bracket"></i> Open Staff Workspace</button></div></section>
